"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101792","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101792","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101792.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101792.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-19T13:04:27Z"},"body":"- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101169\r\n- Alternative of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101788\r\n\r\nPredict the time scale from the delta difference so that the fading time does not depend on the input AnimationNode's delta.\r\n\r\nThis breaks compatibility a bit because it changes the behavior of the existing fading time scaled by the downstream time scale. However, since the scaling is specific to NodeOneShot, this should bring it closer to the behavior of other AnimationNodes.\r\n\r\nIt is possible that a strange state may be produced if the timescale is changed during a fade, but since NodeTransiton and StateMachine should have the same problem, I judge that it is not a problem. The case where the timescale is changed during a transition in AtEnd with a fade is quite niche, IMO.\r\n\r\nThe problem of the fade time and end time being out of sync as in #87009, should no longer occur, but the fade duration will change, as explained below (bit change old behavior).","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions"